 note that the removal path has only `dir_name` (the dir is gone, so `doc[0]` cannot be recomputed), and that `docs.ticket_id` is returned by `find_similar` / matched by `exclude_id` (lexical.py:108) — then pick the option whose key is both derivable on the removal path and consistent with the find_similar return contract.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.07,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["catchup.py:198-200 removal path only has `dir_name` in scope; the directory is gone so `reduce_ticket` cannot recompute `doc[0]`, making 'delete under the same key set _reindex uses' not literally achievable on the removal path","catchup.py:171-176 `doc[0]` is derived from `reduce_ticket`, which requires the directory to still exist","lexical.py:101-108 `docs.ticket_id` is the value returned by find_similar and compared against `exclude_id`; re-keying docs on dir_name (option B) would change that returned identity","The plan states the goal is 'a single documented key governs both' but does not reason through which of the two options is actually viable given the removal path's limited inputs and the find_similar return contract"],"finding":"AC3 offers two fix options as interchangeable, but each carries an unaddressed mechanism constraint: option A (removal path uses _reindex's key set) is infeasible as literally stated because a removed directory can no longer be reduced to recover doc[0]/ticket_id — the removal path structurally has only dir_name; option B (docs keys on dir_name) changes the value stored as docs.ticket_id, which find_similar returns and compares against exclude_id (lexical.py:108), risking a result-identity / self-exclusion regression.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fe65157d9dc5c5ee3","impact":0.67,"is_primary":null,"location":"Acceptance criteria, AC3 ('Either the removal path deletes under the same key set _reindex uses, or docs carries the directory name and both paths key on it')","norm_id":"nc040fcb57560bbdd","priority":0.67,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Implementer picks option A and discovers the removal path cannot compute the ticket_id key, then improvises an inconsistent fix","Implementer picks option B and silently changes what find_similar returns / what exclude_id matches for divergent-name tickets"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Prefer making the removal path mirror _reindex by deleting docs under both the dir_name AND, where recoverable, the stored key — e.g. have dirstate carry the indexed ticket_id so removal can delete by the same key _reindex inserted under, without needing to reduce a vanished directory; state that recovered key as the single governing key in the docstring.","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"medium","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"moderate","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":null,"blocking_enabled":null,"checklist_item":"","cohort":null,"criteria":["P6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":null,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["2 criterion line(s) bundle multiple deliverables with 'and' (split so each is independently verifiable)."],"finding":"Acce